# Code owners for tracktime.
#
# One maintainer today, so the catch-all below already covers every file. The
# explicit entries after it exist for a different reason: they are the paths
# where a wrong change is expensive and hard to notice in review, so they are
# listed by name to make the request unmissable and to say why the path is
# sensitive. Order matters — the last matching pattern wins.
#
# Being an owner is a review request, not a gate. Branch protection is what
# would make these required; see CONTRIBUTING.md for how a PR actually lands.

*                                   @trebeljahr

# --- Authentication and workspace scoping -----------------------------------
# auth.ts configures better-auth including the bearer plugin, so a cookie
# client and a token client (extension, Raycast, CLI) converge on one session
# path. workspace.ts decides which workspace a request may read, and
# client-label.ts is the allowlist of device-flow client ids. A mistake here is
# a cross-account data leak, not a bug report.
/packages/server/src/auth/          @trebeljahr

# --- Express middleware ordering --------------------------------------------
# The order in createApp() is load-bearing and documented in CLAUDE.md
# ("Critical Middleware Ordering"): CORS before every route so preflight works,
# the better-auth handler before express.json because it parses its own body,
# and the scoped import body limit before the global 100kb one because
# whichever json parser runs first consumes the body. Rearranged, most of this
# still boots and fails later, in production.
/packages/server/src/app.ts         @trebeljahr

# --- CI, release and deploy automation --------------------------------------
# build-and-deploy.yml holds the registry push and the Coolify deploy, and the
# release workflows publish artifacts. A change here can ship or break
# production without touching a line of application code.
/.github/workflows/                 @trebeljahr

# --- Licensing and trademark ------------------------------------------------
# AGPL-3.0-or-later, and a trademark policy that is deliberately separate from
# it. Neither is a routine edit; both change what other people are allowed to
# do with this project.
/LICENSE                            @trebeljahr
/TRADEMARK.md                       @trebeljahr

# --- Server environment contract --------------------------------------------
# .env.example is the reference every deployment is built from. The same
# pattern covers .env.production, which is committed with its secrets encrypted
# by dotenvx (it is not present in this checkout). .env.keys is gitignored and
# must stay that way.
/packages/server/.env*              @trebeljahr

# --- Deployment topology ----------------------------------------------------
# The service names `client` and `server` inside these files are load-bearing:
# Coolify keys docker_compose_domains by them, and a mismatch serves 503.
# docker-compose.dev.yml is the local Mongo/Redis/S3 stack that dev and E2E
# both assume; docker-compose.yml is the legacy single-app layout kept for
# reference.
/docker-compose.client.yml          @trebeljahr
/docker-compose.server.yml          @trebeljahr
/docker-compose.dev.yml             @trebeljahr
/docker-compose.yml                 @trebeljahr
